    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d919">

                <pb facs="0830" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg714"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/15230.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State ad interim to the Brazilian
                        Minister to Mexico</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-16T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 16, 1915—6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>784. Your 631, June 12, 5 p.m. Silliman telegraphs that Foreign Office requests
                    him to express thanks of Carranza to Department and to you for good offices in
                    transmitting message of Cházaro and to say there is no reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
